Codex work order: 50x.html (static, no scaling)
Directory + filenames

Create in your repo (source):

~/dox/st33v.com/forge/script/50x/

Output files:

50x/
  README.md
  50x.html
  50x.css


You (St33v)  will deploy to:

/srv/www/st33v.com/50x.html

/srv/www/st33v.com/assets/50x.png

Requirements

Page background is solid black.

The image is displayed at its native size (1920×1080). No responsive scaling.

If viewport is smaller than the image, allow scrollbars (default behavior is fine).

Center the image horizontally and vertically when possible (but still no scaling).

Include minimal accessible text for screen readers (visually hidden).

No external fonts. No JS.

50x.html content (Codex should implement)

Standard HTML5 boilerplate

<link rel="stylesheet" href="/50x.css">

<main> contains:

<img src="/assets/50x.png" width="1920" height="1080" alt="5xx: The machine has encountered turbulence. Please try again shortly.">

Optional: a visually hidden <h1>Server error</h1> and <p>.

50x.css content (Codex should implement)

html, body { height: 100%; margin: 0; background: #000; }

Centering container:

body { display: grid; place-items: center; }

Ensure no scaling:

img { display: block; width: 1920px; height: 1080px; max-width: none; max-height: none; }

Add a “visually hidden” utility class:

.sr-only {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  padding: 0;
  margin: -1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip: rect(0,0,0,0);
  white-space: nowrap;
  border: 0;
}

README.md instructions (Codex should include)
Deploy

Copy to web root:

50x.html → /srv/www/st33v.com/50x.html

50x.css → /srv/www/st33v.com/50x.css

assets/50x.png → /srv/www/st33v.com/assets/50x.png

Nginx config

In the correct server {} block:

error_page 500 502 503 504 /50x.html;

location = /50x.html {
    # internal;  # optional: uncomment if you only want it served as an error handler
}


This is the canonical pattern used in nginx examples.

